@meta
id: 16-20
title: Scenario — partial refunds
chapter: 16
type: scenario
skills: buffer-switch, split-window, window-nav, buffer-list, search-slash, find-f, open-o
par: 640
minutes: 18
vscode: Ctrl-P four times, two of them for files you did not know you needed
open: order.provider.ts payment.service.ts order.entity.ts registry.ts

@brief
A ticket, not an exercise, and two of the files it needs are not open.

    ORD-611  Support want to refund part of an order. A refund larger
             than the order total must be rejected with
             REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL. Expose it as refundOrder on the
             resolver.

  1. `order.provider.ts` — a new method directly after `cancel`, with
     a blank line before it:

         public async refundPartial(id: string, amount: number) {
           const order = await this.findOne(id);

           if (amount > order.total) {
             throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
           }

           return this.paymentService.refund(order.id, amount);
         }

  2. `payment.service.ts` — `refund` takes an optional amount:
     `refund(orderId: string, amount?: number)`, and passes it on in
     the body: `{ orderId, amount }`.

  3. `errors.json` — not open. Add, directly above `REFUND_FAILED`:

         "REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL": { "statusCode": 422, "sentry": false },

  4. `order.resolver.ts` — not open. A new method directly after
     `cancelOrder`, with a blank line before it:

         public async refundOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string; amount: number }) {
           return this.orderProvider.refundPartial(args.id, args.amount);
         }

  5. `order.entity.ts` and `registry.ts` — open, and unchanged. The
     entity has nothing to add and the resolver is already registered.

@keys
| `:b pay` | the service |
| `:sp errors.json` `:sp order.resolver.ts` | the two you have to open yourself |
| `:wq` in a split | write that buffer and close that window |
| `Ctrl-W o` | back to one window if it gets crowded |
| `:ls` | what is loaded, what is `+` |
| `:wqa` | write everything, everywhere, and leave |

@hints
Provider: `G` is the closing brace of the class, `k` is the closing
brace of `cancel`. `o` there, `Enter` for the blank line, then type
the method. Leading spaces are autoindent's job; closing braces dedent
themselves.
--
Service: `/refund(` then `f)` and `i` for the parameter. `/orderId }`
lands on `orderId`; `e` then `a` appends after it.
--
The two files you open: `:sp errors.json`, `/FAILED`, `O`, the line,
`Esc`, `:wq`. `:sp order.resolver.ts`, `G`, `k`, `o`, `Enter`, the
method, `Esc`, `:wq`. Each `:wq` closes only the split.
--
`:ls` before you leave. Four buffers from the command line, two you
added; the entity and the registry must show no `+`. Then `:wqa`.

@solution
A reasonable route.

**order.provider.ts** — `G` `k` `o` `Enter`, then the method, one
line per Enter, no leading spaces, `Esc`, `:w`.

**payment.service.ts** — `:b pay`. `/refund(` `Enter`, `f)`, `i`,
`, amount?: number`, `Esc`. `/orderId }` `Enter`, `e`, `a`,
`, amount`, `Esc`.

**errors.json** — `:sp errors.json`. `/FAILED` `Enter`, `O`, the
entry, `Esc`, `:wq`.

**order.resolver.ts** — `:sp order.resolver.ts`. `G` `k` `o` `Enter`,
the method, `Esc`, `:wq`.

`:wqa`.

Around five hundred and sixty keystrokes, and all but about fifty of
them are the code the ticket asked for. Everything the chapter added,
the buffer hop, the two splits, the two `:wq` that close a window and
not vim, comes to under forty.

That ratio is the point. In VS Code this ticket is four tabs, two
Ctrl-P searches, and a moment of "which tab was the resolver". Here
the files you were given are a fragment away and the files you were
not given are a `:sp` away, and the layout never gets in the way of
the code. A window opened for one edit closes with the same `:wq` you
were going to type anyway.

The trap is the pair of decoys. A ticket that says "expose it on the
resolver" makes you want to open the registry and add a line, and the
line is already there. Read before you type. The buffer list is cheap;
a change to a file that did not need one is not.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async refundPartial(id: string, amount: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    return this.paymentService.refund(order.id, amount);
  }
}

@start payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/refunds`, { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string, amount?: number) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/refunds`, { orderId, amount });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@start order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start registry.ts
import { container } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderRepository } from '../domain/order/order.repository';
import { OrderProvider } from '../domain/order/order.provider';
import { OrderResolver } from '../domain/order/order.resolver';
import { PaymentService } from '../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

container.register('OrderRepository', { useClass: OrderRepository });
container.register('OrderProvider', { useClass: OrderProvider });
container.register('PaymentService', { useClass: PaymentService });
container.register('OrderResolver', { useClass: OrderResolver });

